WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.250
Natsu!

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.320
Follow your instinct! You're a striker, aren't you?!

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.250
Ah, so close!

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.250
It's not over, follow up!

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.500
That's not far enough, get it up front!

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.760
Akasaki! Let me shoot!

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.260
It's Natsuki! Lima, block him!

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.140
Oh shi-

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.820
Yeah!

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:56.780
He scored!

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.780
Nice, Akasaki! Good job, man!

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.540
Zaki!

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.790
How's that?! Did you see that?!

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.710
Yeah! Great goal, Akasaki!

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.800
Now we're back in the game!

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.660
Zaki, nice goal!

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.800
Akasaki!

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:04.950
They managed to grab a goal even with an iron-wall defense.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.870
This is getting interesting.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.240
We can do this, manager!

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:16.480
Now, can ETU start to gain momentum?

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.260
That was a great shot!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.260
So nice!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.640
G-Gino...

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.140
Geez.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.510
It only went well because they weren't able to clear the ball properly.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.650
We almost blew that chance.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.200
And that's after my loyal dog orchestrated a great attack,

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.020
Right, Baki?

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:48.910
Yes?

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:53.660
It's annoying when naive people do naive things, but

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.170
if they're doing things half-heartedly, it's even worse.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:07.800
Since you're on my team, at least put in a bit more effort, Natsu.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.310
Gino... He's so stuck-up!

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.560
Natsu, your shot was crucial.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.680
Thanks to that, they focused on you, which created an opening for me.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.320
So it was somewhat an assist.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.700
A-Akasaki!

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.980
But still, it only went in because of my skill.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.080
Alright! Let's keep this up and grab an equalizer!

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.580
Yeah!

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.810
Right, that's it.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:53.550
When I shoot, I'm also maximizing my teammates' potential!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:00.370
Though I still don't know what the manager meant by "resolve as a forward",

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:05.520
I want to remain as a forward who always goes for the goal.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.990
Actually,

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:12.370
I'm not confident I could do anything but that...

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.300
I hope the manager isn't mad at me.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:26.570
I'm so happy! I'm so happy, Sera!

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.800
What? That's creepy!

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.560
They finally managed to get one back.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:39.660
20 minutes left. This will be really rough for ETU.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.540
The dominant Osaka will definitely push for a win here.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.070
Dulfer is making his move.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.020
Now what will you do, Tatsumi?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.580
Can you get two more goals against them?

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:59.570
Number 4, Ootomo. He normally plays as a defensive midfielder...

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:02.820
It looks like Kubota's gonna be subbed off.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.580
Alright.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.230
Kubota's going out.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.840
The excellent Kubota's getting subbed.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.870
Well done, Kubota!

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.350
Yeah! We're counting on you next time!

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.870
Though he didn't beat me,

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.110
he's really got something.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.470
If this guy gets more experience,

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:38.620
he might become a terrifying player.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:39.870
Good job.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.910
Man, it's so sad.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:51.090
It feels like being forced to go home while my friends are still playing.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:58.390
You played very well, Kubota.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.170
This is your best performance so far this season.

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.650
Uh...umm...thanks.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:12.600
Take a rest on the bench and cheer the team on from there.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.410
Yes.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:27.170
To be honest, I wanted to use him for another 10 minutes...

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:35.320
My best performance so far, huh?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.430
That was no good.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.740
When you don't play a full game, half the fun is gone.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.290
As I thought, I really have to work on my stamina.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.940
They have it good; they can still play.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.450
I'm envious...

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.300
That Kubota had me sweating for a bit.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.200
I didn't think he was that good a player.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:06.210
It's going just as we planned, eh?

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.510
Kubota has never been a player who runs around to get the ball.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.950
Using Sugie who's an expert at man-marking against him

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.380
wasn't just to make sure he doesn't get the loose balls,

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.350
it's also to wear Kubota out?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.460
Kubota got one over Sugie.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:31.980
I wasn't expecting that, but that was a double-edged sword.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:36.940
Since he was upbeat, he was running more than usual.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:39.830
But he ended up wearing himself out earlier than we expected.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.270
Now Osaka's loose ball recovery rate will drop.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:50.000
They now have no choice but to ditch their usual ultra-attacking style.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.260
Shimura has pushed up now.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.530
Tatsumi Takeshi,

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:03.770
If you think that we'll stop attacking just because we took off a forward,

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.690
you couldn't be more wrong.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.770
Let's halt their momentum, Shimura.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:14.980
Let me teach you a lesson, Dulfer.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.800
They aren't committing many players for an attack.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:35.220
There aren't that many players, like Shimura,

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.090
who're able to remain focused and calm throughout the entire game.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:42.570
What's he scheming?

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:48.310
Why is it so hot?

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:52.990
I thought it'll be cooler at night so I wore long sleeves,

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.940
but you get hot when you run around.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.740
That's when you have to roll your sleeves up.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.700
Though the bunched up part will be kinda uncomfortable,

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.320
it still feels better than before.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:06.390
Adapting to situations like this,

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.210
I bet that's how humans evolved.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.210
What the hell is he babbling about?

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:16.960
Adapting to situations applies to soccer as well.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:22.340
ETU's fast players are still full of energy,

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.600
so to do a counter will be hard.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.160
That's why you have to launch a simple attack...

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.060
...without committing too many people.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.690
They're using the flanks! Are they trying to beat us with speed?!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.170
Go, Hatake!

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:49.040
Don't let ETU get cocky!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.790
There's not much time left. I'll just let Hauer grab the glory!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.670
Make it count, Hauer!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.950
He's jumping in with his whole body!

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.170
Kuroda!

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:10.780
It's weak!

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:12.180
But it's heading for goal!

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:17.570
Okay!

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.530
Yeah, Sugie!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.190
Nice cover!

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:25.490
Man, that was kinda dangerous!

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.780
Sugie!

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:31.700
Alright!

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:35.710
What the hell, Hauer?! I expected more from you!

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.920
Haha, good one Sugie!

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.090
Nice clear!

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:47.510
You've been irritating me all game!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.350
Cut it out already!

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:50.600
Referee!

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.360
Hauer got a yellow card?!

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:04.820
Hey, wait a minute! He should get one before me!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:04.990
Let it go, Hauer!
Hey, wait a minute! He should get one before me!

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:05.280
Let it go, Hauer!

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.360
He ran into me first! Why do I get a yellow card instead?!

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:11.100
I understand how you feel.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:14.370
Hau-chan has entered his rebellious phase.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:17.330
Nice, what a bargain.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:20.630
I was right to pit Kuro against Hauer.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.130
I didn't think he'd get that pissed.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:26.930
I guess Kuro has a talent at pissing people off.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:30.640
Kuroda will be hurt when he hears that...

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.520
Well, I think it's time for us to make our move.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:44.010
Damn, my legs are worn out.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.040
I guess that can't be helped.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.780
I had to run all game just to keep up with Tsubaki.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:57.630
That run just then...

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.890
I have heard about him during the meeting.

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:02.870
Seems like there's a real need to watch out for Tsubaki after all.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:05.760
Once he gets going, he's unstoppable.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:15.130
Damn, it's in a weird place again!

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:20.070
Tsubaki... I can't let him get the ball!

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.740
Wait, am I being forced to run?

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:32.320
Our ball!

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.700
No way, that couldn't be...

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:46.030
Oh, ETU's making a change too!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.340
Tanba is coming in for Kiyokawa!

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:50.600
Alright. Good work, Kiyo!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:52.080
Leave the rest to me!

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:52.840
Okay.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.850
Ootomo! Ootomo!

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:59.080
Good. Well done, Kiyokawa.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:13:59.730
Thanks.

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:07.750
Dulfer should have noticed by now.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.110
Well then, what are you going to do?

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:16.270
Tanba is going straight to the left full-back position.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:21.480
It seems like ETU have been concentrating their attacks on the left side.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:27.880
But Gino's passes are always being cut off by Hiraga's hard work.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:32.270
So much that it seems unnatural...

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.740
To be honest,

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:41.330
Gino has delivered some good passes, for someone who's not on form today.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:45.270
But if he intended to make me run...

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:52.250
If he placed his passes right where Tsubaki and I have to battle for the ball...

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:54.780
it means that he...

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.790
...might actually be on form today.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:04.170
But then what's with that face?

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:10.540
If he planned this, why would he look so displeased?

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.270
Are you alright, Akasaki?!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.590
It hurts!

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.830
Man, this is tough.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:43.080
When I first heard about this plan, I thought it sounded fun.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:47.080
But when I started doing it, problems began to surface.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:55.720
My pass completion rate goes down...

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:59.470
...when I intentionally put them in weird places.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.720
It really frustrates me.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:09.220
As I thought, Gino wasn't having an off day.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:14.750
He made that face because he was thinking about his pass completion rate.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.240
Damn it, I was tricked!

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:25.450
It looks like even Hiraga is getting a bit tired.

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.630
Manager?

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:41.920
Where is that spark you had at the beginning, Dulfer?

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.670
Are you worried about something?

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:47.640
Well, just stay that way.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:54.230
The time you spend worrying will be our time to shine.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:04.990
Oh, now I see! So that's how it is, Monsieur Tatsumi!

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:06.370
What?

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:09.500
Hmm, yes, I see.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:14.000
The target's been Hiraga all along.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.510
I knew he was plotting something.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:22.760
I didn't think that the No. 10, Gino, would keep making the same mistake.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.810
But, his purpose was to...

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:29.270
make use of ETU's speedy No.7...

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:33.020
to wear Hiraga out.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:38.860
Hiraga is a player who believes in hard work

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:41.660
and he's willing to use up all of his energy in a game.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:46.030
And so, by forcing him to keep running during the first half,

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.540
his energy allocation's messed up.

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:56.000
Disabling Hiraga's wide area of defensive coverage...

00:17:56.300 --> 00:18:00.550
...basically means that ETU have conquered that part of the pitch.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:12.830
How much stamina does this guy have?!

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.370
This is our chance!

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:17.730
Sera!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:20.910
Oh, too bad!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.110
It's still available! Go for it!

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:26.490
Hey, what are you doing? Don't let them do whatever they want!

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.670
It's true! Katayama has no choice but to go back to defend!

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.180
It's just like what the manager has said!

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:37.630
If that's the case, this could actually work!

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.630
Monsieur Blanc,

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:43.800
then why not sub Hiraga off?

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.510
Against a fresh player, ETU would have a harder time, right?

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.770
That's the interesting part.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.580
According to my information,

00:18:56.580 --> 00:19:00.060
Hiraga has missed a few games due to suspensions or injuries,

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.280
but, other than that, he's never been subbed off since Dulfer took charge.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:07.030
Osaka is a team where the starting players are fixed.

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:13.510
The substitution patterns are mostly fixed as well.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.540
Instead of adapting to their opponent's playing style,

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:21.110
they stand by their philosophy.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:24.420
It's a team that's as confident as Dulfer himself..

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:30.430
That's exactly the reason as to why they can't take out Hiraga.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:34.940
Hiraga is their captain and, as such, he's irreplaceable.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.310
He's the one who emphasizes Dulfer's ideals on the pitch.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:38.940
You're too lax there! Focus!

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:44.690
Will he take out a player like him in order to win the match?

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:52.200
Or will they stick to their ideals that will go a long way in the future?

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.100
I believe Dulfer is having quite a dilemma.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:20:00.460
The one's having a good time on the other hand...

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.710
...is Monsieur Tatsumi.

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:06.180
Oh, I see.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:16.100
I wasn't mistaken. You're an interesting man, Monsieur Tatsumi.

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:22.800
Alright, we're almost caught up! Go ETU!

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:24.440
Hey, Shige.

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:25.360
Huh?

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:29.610
It's stupid to just carry this thing, so how about holding it up?

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:33.370
Oh, sure. Let's do it!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.620
I haven't seen it anyway.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.800
Does it say "Edo style fan troupe"?

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:40.620
Huh? No.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:43.100
Does it say "Tatsumi" then?

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.330
No...

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:53.390
Tsu-Tsubaki?

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:57.540
Well, there is no banner for him.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.510
But...

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:05.650
I just get the feeling that he'll be incredible one day.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.900
Since it's already been made,

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:18.160
we have no choice but to cheer for him.

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:21.610
Go! Tsubaki!

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:23.490
Go!

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.630
Tsubaki!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.920
Go, Tsubaki!

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:33.600
Huh? Aren't those our dads?

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.550
Why are they holding a Tsubaki banner? I don't get it.

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.070
But, at this rate, Tsubaki might just create an opening. Well then...

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.730
Tsubaki!

00:21:47.730 --> 00:21:49.490
Show us something special!

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.070
Go!

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:53.910
Gino!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:57.590
I just need to shut this guy down!

00:21:58.140 --> 00:22:02.930
You don't get it, there's no point in watching me now.

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:04.960
Here, Tanbee!

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:12.740
Looks like we don't have that much time left.

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:15.890
Make this one count, Tsubaki!

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:24.100
Nice pass, Tanba!

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:26.110
Go, Tsubaki!

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:36.240
He's fast!

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:39.240
Wind? Or is it a torpedo?

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:41.620
Hiraga!

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:44.920
This will work!

00:22:45.310 --> 00:22:46.540
Natsu?

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:47.920
Sera?

00:22:48.610 --> 00:22:50.300
Or myself!

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:51.970
Okay!

00:24:15.460 --> 00:24:18.190
In order to catch up, we've got to exploit this.

00:24:18.190 --> 00:24:20.050
How can we lose to you guys?!

00:24:20.050 --> 00:24:21.190
We are out of time!

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:23.780
You're the only one who can settle this matter.

00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:28.340
Maybe believing in a player like myself is fine after all!
